{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791048586,"nonce":"qIu/PNlrHBz4hO+AlSzN22UIges=","title":"blinc_core::Shadow cannot grow fields while packages/* pin exhaustive literals","message":"e15ee566 added `pub inset: bool` to `blinc_core::Shadow`. That is a\nbreaking change for every downstream that writes an exhaustive struct\nliteral, and `blinc_node_editor` writes two:\n\n    src/render.rs   fn tinted_glow(..) -\u003e blinc_core::Shadow\n    src/theme.rs    fn port_shadow(\u0026self) -\u003e blinc_core::Shadow\n\nThe root Cargo.toml patches `blinc_core` to the local path for the\n`project-blinc/Blinc.git` URL, while `blinc_node_editor` itself stays\npinned at a git rev (abcc7da). So the pinned editor compiles against\nHEAD's `blinc_core` and nothing bumps with it. Main went red at\ne15ee566 and stayed red for three more commits: CI, Documentation and\nCoverage all failed with the same two E0063s. Android and iOS Compile\npassed, because neither enables the `node-editor` feature.\n\n\nIt did, eventually. The cargo git checkout at\n\n    ~/.cargo/git/checkouts/blinc_node_editor-8110bffc32a835f1/abcc7da/\n\nhad been hand-edited to add `inset: false` to both literals. A local\n`cargo check -p blinc_app_examples --features node-editor` therefore\npassed against a source tree that does not exist in the repository.\nDeleting the checkout and letting cargo re-extract reproduced CI\nexactly.\n\nNever edit a cargo checkout to get a build green. It is global, it\nsurvives `cargo clean`, and it silently decouples the local build from\nevery other machine's.\n\n\n1. Fix the two literals in `blinc_node_editor`, push, bump the rev.\n   Correct, but needs a cross-repo push and leaves the same trap for\n   the next field.\n2. Keep the flag only where nothing downstream constructs the type.\n   Chosen. `blinc_theme::Shadow` is never built by literal outside\n   `blinc_theme`, so the flag stays there; `blinc_core::Shadow` goes\n   back to five fields and the two kinds travel in separate lists\n   (`ElementStyle::inner_shadow`, `RenderProps::inner_shadow`).\n\nThe split also removes a per-layer branch from the paint walk, which\nnow iterates one list before the fill and the other after.\n\n\n`blinc_core` types reachable from a `packages/*` literal are part of a\npinned ABI. Adding a field to one is a cross-repo change. Either mark\nthe struct `#[non_exhaustive]` (and give it a constructor downstream can\nreach) or keep new state in a type the packages do not construct.\nRelated: 12cb642 on pins building two copies of a shared crate.","files":null}]}